---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service">
  <section class="max-w-4xl w-full mx-auto px-6 py-12 text-gray-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-gray-600">
      Medeligo Cancer Research provides a specialized search engine that helps clinicians,
      researchers, and informed patients discover oncology-focused publications.
      By accessing or using our services, you agree to comply with the terms outlined below.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        Your use of Medeligo constitutes acceptance of this agreement. If you do not agree
        with any part of these terms, you must discontinue use of the platform immediately.
        We may update these terms periodically to reflect changes in our services or
        applicable regulations. Continued use after updates signifies acceptance of the
        revised terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">2. Purpose of the Service</h2>
      <p>
        Medeligo indexes and synthesizes publicly available medical research to aid
        discovery. We do not author medical content, provide medical advice, or guarantee
        the completeness of external sources. You are solely responsible for evaluating the
        quality, accuracy, and applicability of any information surfaced through the
        service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">3. Medical Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Our platform is intended for informational purposes only. It does not replace
        the independent judgment of licensed medical professionals. Medeligo, its team,
        and partners are not liable for decisions or outcomes based on the information
        presented on this site. Always consult qualified healthcare providers before
        applying any medical knowledge or treatment recommendations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">4. User Responsibilities</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
        <li>Use the platform only for lawful research and educational purposes.</li>
        <li>Respect intellectual property rights associated with referenced publications.</li>
        <li>Maintain the confidentiality of any account credentials used to access
          additional features.</li>
        <li>Report suspected misuse or security incidents to our support team promptly.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">5. Analytics and Data Usage</h2>
      <p>
        We employ analytics tools to understand how the platform is used so we can improve
        search quality and user experience. These tools may collect usage metrics such as
        query patterns, device information, and general location data. We do not share user
        information with third parties other than trusted analytics providers operating on
        our behalf under strict confidentiality obligations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">6. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        Medeligo owns all proprietary features, branding, and interface materials on this
        site. Third-party research articles and metadata remain the property of their
        respective authors and publishers. You may not copy, redistribute, or sell any part
        of our platform without prior written permission except where permitted by law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">7. Service Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We strive to maintain reliable access to our tools; however, service interruptions
        may occur due to maintenance, updates, or events outside our control. Medeligo is
        not responsible for losses arising from downtime, delays, or data inaccuracies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Medeligo and its affiliates shall not be
        liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages
        resulting from your use of the platform, reliance on search results, or inability to
        access the service. This limitation applies even if we have been advised of the
        possibility of such damages.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">9. Changes to the Service</h2>
      <p>
        We may modify or discontinue features, algorithms, or content sources without prior
        notice. Significant changes to these terms will be communicated through our site.
        Your continued use after such changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about these Terms of Service, please contact our team at
        <a class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700" href="mailto:support@medeligo.com">
          support@medeligo.com
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
